<title>USA: High Plains Wheat - Dealers shrug off cold snap.</title>
<headline>High Plains Wheat - Dealers shrug off cold snap.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Grain merchandisers in the U.S. High Plains said Friday they were not worried that a current cold snap would pose a threat to the hard red winter wheat crop.</p>
<p>&quot;It's in the 20s (Farenheit) now and supposed to get into the teens tonight,&quot; a south central Kansas dealer said. &quot;At this level and stage where the wheat's at, there's no big concern.&quot;</p>
<p>Meanwhile, basis bids for hard red winter wheat were mostly unchanged, and movement of wheat was slow.  </p>
